{"commit": "32fc82ba953a93ff2cae78be5d78595078c67193", "id": "32fc82ba953a93ff2cae78be5d78595078c67193-1", "language": "rust", "reason": "Selected test is not present at the fixed revision: raw::tests::fst_map_many3", "repo": "https://github.com/BurntSushi/fst", "reproduction": {"attempt": "20260924T001754Z-9a8f7c49", "evidence_sha256": {"evidence/32fc82ba953a93ff2cae78be5d78595078c67193-1/20260924T001754Z-9a8f7c49/origin.json": "64e1bf4a2094fe064d71b1198d9c7438c209c6fb1a0b8bd391d985933b08e545", "evidence/32fc82ba953a93ff2cae78be5d78595078c67193-1/20260924T001754Z-9a8f7c49/proposal.json": "6abb753cfabf9c7f5bd9fe29f4c4740b618d28b92843b04a85ed2338c0f233fd"}, "provenance": "verbatim"}, "shard": "fst", "status": "blocked", "subject": "Fix output value bug.", "summary": "Pre-fix `Builder::insert_output` took an `Output` value and treated `Output::zero()` as 'no output', so a non-zero entry whose key was a strict prefix of a later zero-valued entry never had its output relocated to a final-output slot when the prefix was extended. Result: `Map::get` returns the wrong value for the prefix key. The fix changes the internal API to `Option<Output>`, distinguishing 'zero output' from 'no output'.", "updated_at": "2026-09-24T00:17:54.917694+00:00"}
